<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/070P">Remark <span data-tag="070P">9.7.3.16</span> <span class="named">(Size Estimates for Tensor Products)</span>.</a> Let $\kappa &lt; \lambda $ be regular cardinals, let $\mathbb {K}$ be a collection of $\kappa $-small simplicial sets, and let $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ be $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete $\infty $-categories. If $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ are essentially $\lambda $-small and $\lambda $ has exponential cofinality $\geq \kappa $, then the $\mathbb {K}$-cocomplete tensor product $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K} } \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is also essentially $\lambda $-small. By virtue of Remark <a data-tag="070F" href="/tag/070F">9.7.3.8</a>, this is a special case of Corollary <a data-tag="06ZW" href="/tag/06ZW">9.7.1.15</a>. </p>
<p>In particular, if $\mathbb {K}$ is a small collection of small simplicial sets and the $\infty $-categories $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ and $\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ are essentially small, then $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\otimes _{ \mathbb {K}} \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ is also essentially small. </p>
</article>
